{"_meta":{"securitySchemes":[{"scopes":["openid","profile","email"],"type":"oauth2"}]},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":true,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"Call one Bowmark function and keep the session open for the next call"},"description":"Runs ONE library function in a Bowmark session, so a flow that needs several calls in the SAME session can finish: a booking that texts the user a code, a cart filled over several steps, a form that waits on an answer from the user. `run` cannot do these, because every run starts fresh and nothing it held survives to the next run.

